# 1. Objective

The objective of this phase is to establish a documented, evidence-based baseline of GeFlow AI's existing user interface, user experience, application functionality, business logic, navigation, data flows, integrations, permissions, and operational workflows.

This baseline will serve as the reference point for all future implementation work, particularly the integration of 29 dedicated AI agents for GeFlow's 29 business categories.

Before any new agent-related development begins, the builder must understand and document how the existing application currently behaves.

The baseline must protect:

- Existing page layouts and component structures.
- Existing colors, typography, spacing, icons, and visual styles.
- Existing navigation and routing.
- Existing authentication and account management.
- Existing dashboard functionality.
- Existing business-category and product-category management.
- Existing unit-of-measurement management.
- Existing purchasing and supplier workflows.
- Existing inventory management.
- Existing POS and sales workflows.
- Existing reporting and analytics.
- Existing billing, subscription, and pricing functionality.
- Existing administrative interfaces.
- Existing permissions and security controls.
- Existing database structures and data relationships.
- Existing APIs and integrations.
- Existing responsive behavior.
- Existing loading, error, success, and empty states.

**Core rule: New AI capabilities must integrate with the existing GeFlow application. They must not silently redesign, replace, remove, or damage existing functionality.**

