# 5. Baseline Classification System

Every discovered page, feature, workflow, and relevant component must receive a clear status.

Use these classifications:

### A. Working and Verified

The feature was inspected and its relevant behavior was successfully verified.

### B. Partially Working

Some functionality works, but at least one required operation is incomplete or failing.

### C. Broken

A reproducible failure prevents the feature from behaving as expected.

### D. Implemented but Unverified

Relevant implementation exists, but its runtime behavior could not be safely verified.

### E. Planned but Not Implemented

Documentation or planning references the feature, but there is no sufficient evidence that it exists in the running application.

### F. Not Found

The feature was not found in the inspected application or project sources.

### G. Blocked

Verification requires access, credentials, infrastructure, permission, or another dependency that is unavailable.

### H. Requires Further Investigation

Available evidence is insufficient to assign a more precise status.

Every classification must include evidence or an explicit explanation of the verification limitation.

